This is 99% Invisible. I'm Roman Mars. After the revolution in Cuba, the young Fidel Castro hired an official photographer by the name of Alberto Cora to chronicle his new life as a national leader. Cora followed Castro and Che Guevara, taking pictures of them as they met world leaders, went fishing, faced off in chess. He even took that iconic image of Che, the one that's on millions of t-shirts.
这里是《99%隐形》。我是罗曼·马尔斯。古巴革命后，年轻的菲德尔·卡斯特罗聘请了一位名叫阿尔贝托·科尔达的官方摄影师，来记录他作为国家领导人的新生活。科尔达跟随卡斯特罗和切·格瓦拉，拍摄了他们会见世界领导人、钓鱼、下棋的照片。他还拍下了那张标志性的切·格瓦拉照片，就是印在数百万件T恤上的那张。

