And there was a special fountain in the main piata. And in the piata, I placed a sculpture I did. Just like a fruit called papaya, that in Cuba has this sexual feminine connotation. Some higher ups found this pretty scandalous. Poro was told to turn the water in the fountain off. Yes, you have the breast, and here you have the papaya, which is a metaphor for what everybody knows in the Caribbean. But I think that it's wrong to overemphasize that.
主广场上有一个特殊的喷泉。在广场上，我放置了我做的一件雕塑。就像一种叫木瓜的水果，在古巴，它具有这种性感的女性内涵。一些高层觉得这很丢人。波罗被告知要关掉喷泉里的水。是的，你有乳房，这里有木瓜，这是加勒比地区众所周知的隐喻。但我认为过度强调这一点是错误的。

