priority than, say, creating the most beautiful art schools in the world. So there was the money issue, but also generally generally, Cuba was starting to imitate the Soviet Union in more and more ways. I made a very individual architecture and they wanted Soviet architecture. The Soviet architecture was blocky, functional, uniform, one-size-fits-all, completely the opposite of the sensuous, organic vaults and curves of the art schools. There was an idea that the designs for the Cuban National Art Schools were extravagant for a socialist revolution that had to tighten its belt. And one of the earliest proponents of that argument was Roberto Segre.
优先级。所以存在资金问题，但总的来说，古巴开始在越来越多的方面模仿苏联。我做的是非常个人化的建筑，而他们想要苏联式的建筑。苏联建筑是方块状的、功能性的、统一的、千篇一律的，与艺术学校感性、有机的拱顶和曲线完全相反。有一种观点认为，古巴国家艺术学校的设计对于一个必须勒紧裤腰带的社会主义革命来说太奢侈了。而这一论点的最早支持者之一是罗伯托·塞格雷。

